{"key":"GorpEquationWindow","text":"## GorpEquationWindow\n\nThe **Gorp Equation Window** is a visual mathematical expression editor.\nBuild equations by combining nodes on an interactive canvas, then save the\nresult as a MathML-compatible Gorp algorithm.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.04 | Right-click for Save to GitHub (persists as Gorp algorithm XML) and Undo/Redo options. Ctrl+Z to undo, Ctrl+Shift+Z to redo (up to 50 steps).\nEquation Canvas | 0.50, 0.50 | Visual expression builder. Click a grey slot to open the slot editor and choose Variable, Literal, Unary, Binary, Comparison, or Logical. Right-click a node to delete, wrap in negation/parentheses/sqrt, or use power-delete options. Double-click a variable or literal to rename/change its value.\n\n---\n\n### Building Expressions\n\n- **Click a slot** (grey placeholder) to open the slot editor\n- In the slot editor, choose a node type:\n  - **Variable** — a named input (e.g. `x`, `count`)\n  - **Literal** — a numeric constant (e.g. `42`, `3.14`)\n  - **Unary** — negation `–`, square root `√`, or parentheses `( )`\n  - **Binary** — `+`, `–`, `×`, `÷`, `^` (power)\n  - **Comparison** — `<`, `>`, `≤`, `≥`, `=`\n  - **Logical** — `AND`, `OR`, `NOT`\n- Each node that accepts operands shows sub-slots for its children\n\n---\n\n### Editing Nodes\n\n- **Click** a node to select it\n- **Right-click** a node for options:\n  - Delete node\n  - Wrap in negation / parentheses / square root\n  - For power nodes: *Delete Power, keep base* / *keep exponent* / *Delete Upwards chain*\n- **Double-click** a variable or literal to rename/change its value\n\n---\n\n### The Library\n\nThe **≡** button on the title bar opens the **Library** pane: every equation in your saved Gorp files, grouped by name (Auth.User.Login lives in Auth.gorp). Click a name to open it; right-click for New, Rename, Delete, Duplicate, Move and Find usages. The chips narrow it to algorithms, models or drafts, and the search box filters by name.\n\n**A name's color is what gorpIT last said about it:**\n- **Green** — the last run was answered and its units agreed\n- **Yellow** — incomplete, answered with a caveat, or a test that is meant to fail\n- **Red** — the run failed, or the units did not match\n- **White** — never run, or changed since its last run (undo the change and the color comes back)\n\nHover a name for the verdict line in the same color. Running never changes the file: the colors are kept with your window, not in the equation.\n\n---\n\n### Units and runs\n\n- Every variable can carry a **unit** (km/h, m/s², mg/dL…), chosen from the unit picker so only valid units can be built. The canvas works out the unit of the answer, and says so when an equation adds seconds to kilograms\n- **Test** evaluates here; **Gorp** sends the equation to the gorpIT service, which answers in the unit the editor declares\n- **⟲ Runs** opens the run log: the expectation (what this equation should produce, saved with it), then your last runs with the exact bytes sent and received\n\n---\n\n### Undo / Redo\n\n- **Ctrl+Z** — undo last change\n- **Ctrl+Shift+Z** — redo\n- **Right-click the canvas background** — shows Undo / Redo options when available\n- History is kept up to **50 steps**\n\n---\n\n### Saving\n\nRight-click the title bar → **Save to GitHub** to persist the equation as\na Gorp algorithm XML file. Closing or minimizing the window, or hiding the browser tab,\nsaves unsaved changes too, as long as the algorithm has a name.\n\n---\n\n### Video\n\nHelp/Videos/GorpEquationWindow.mp4\n\n### Status: Stable\n### Purpose: AIDesign\n\n---","screenshot":""}